//! `written-while-kept` writes a value while its region retains a shared view.
//!
//! An address-shaped self-reference freezes.
//! Exclusive access waits for the region to end. The checker refuses the write
//! as `HeldKept`.
//!
//! The source binds a thunk at `s`. It writes `s`. It then forces the thunk.
//!
//! Rust refuses a write through a value borrowed from itself.
//! - see: #1183 — `writtenWhileKept`

/// `writtenWhileKept` writes its hold while a thunk retains its view.
@[ refuses("HeldKept") ]
def writtenWhileKept() -> Integer =
  var s = 3
  let k : (() -> Integer) at s = access shared s as w { pure thunk { pure w } };
  access s as v { resume v 4 };
  force k
